388	\textbf{Inference cost and deployment.} The router is a Conv1d gate of $853$ parameters ($0.4\%$ of one expert head, ${<}10^{-3}$ of the frozen backbone). With $k{=}2$ of $K{=}5$ experts active per window, RR-MoA adds two adapter forward passes plus the gate to one frozen TSFM forward; the unselected $K{-}k$ experts do not execute. Because the backbone is strictly frozen, a single TSFM held in GPU memory can be shared across many tenants while per-task adapter pools (${\sim}500$K params each) are hot-swapped from host RAM, an arrangement DLinear and per-dataset-from-scratch baselines cannot match (Appendix~\ref{app:benchmark}).
